{"name":"Not a Cloud in Sight","hex":"#85c8d3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"not","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Nomatsiguenga."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Negates the meaning of the modified verb.","To no degree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/not"},{"term":"cloud","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A visible mass of water droplets suspended in the air.","Any mass of dust, steam or smoke resembling such a mass."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become foggy or gloomy, or obscured from sight.","To overspread or hide with a cloud or clouds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloud"},{"term":"sight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sense or faculty by which objects are perceived through the agency of light; the sense by which we see.","An act, instance, opportunity or possibility of seeing; the perception of objects by the eye; view (see also idiomatic expressions such as in sight, out of sight, catch sight of, etc.)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see; to get sight of (something); to register visually.","To observe through, or as if through, a sight, to check the elevation, direction, levelness, or other characteristics of, especially when surveying or navigating."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cloud","blocks":[{"text":"In meteorology, a cloud is an aerosol consisting of a visible mass of miniature liquid droplets, ice crystals, or other particles, suspended in the atmosphere of a planetary body or similar space. Water, primarily, comprises the droplets and crystals. On Earth, clouds are formed as a result of saturation of the air when it is cooled to its dew point, or when it gains sufficient moisture, usually in the form of water vapor, from an adjacent source to raise the dew point to the ambient temperature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons